-- title:
--   A fixed bounded recipe emits the exact raw cyclic circuit
-- statement:
--   Let P be cyclic-compiler metadata with index width k at least 3 and clock parameters satisfying ell=2^c−1. For every raw source instruction list src, evaluating the fixed circuit recipe gives exactly the raw compiler output:
--
--   $$
--   k\ge3,\quad \ell=2^c-1
--   \quad\Longrightarrow\quad
--   \operatorname{program.eval}(P.\mathrm{env},\mathrm{src})
--    =P.\operatorname{compile}(\mathrm{src}).
--   $$
--
--   This is equality of the complete ordered raw circuit data, including its register counts, output address, and instruction list. The recipe uses fixed templates and width-bounded loops; the separate machine theorems establish its polynomial-time evaluation.
